{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# LLM Evaluation \u2014 RAGAS, DeepEval, G-Eval Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: faithfulness with NLI (RAGAS-style)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from typing import Callable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import pipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "nli = pipeline(\"text-classification\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "               model=\"MoritzLaurer/DeBERTa-v3-large-mnli-fever-anli-ling-wanli\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "               top_k=None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# `llm` is any callable: prompt str -> generated str."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Example: llm = lambda p: client.messages.create(model=\"claude-haiku-4-5\", ...).content[0].text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "LLM = Callable[[str], str]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def atomic_claims(answer: str, llm: LLM) -> list[str]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prompt = f\"\"\"Break this answer into simple factual claims (one per line):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "{answer}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return llm(prompt).splitlines()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def faithfulness(answer: str, context: str, llm: LLM) -> float:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    claims = atomic_claims(answer, llm)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not claims:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    supported = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for claim in claims:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        result = nli({\"text\": context, \"text_pair\": claim})[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        entail = next((s for s in result if s[\"label\"] == \"entailment\"), None)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if entail and entail[\"score\"] > 0.5:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            supported += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return supported / len(claims)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Decompose the answer into atomic claims. NLI-check each claim against the retrieved context. Faithfulness = fraction supported."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: answer relevance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# encoder: any model implementing .encode(texts, normalize_embeddings=True) -> ndarray"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# e.g., encoder = SentenceTransformer(\"BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def answer_relevance(question: str, answer: str, encoder, llm: LLM, n: int = 3) -> float:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    prompt = f\"Write {n} questions this answer could be the answer to:\\n{answer}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    generated = [line for line in llm(prompt).splitlines() if line.strip()][:n]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not generated:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    q_emb = np.asarray(encoder.encode([question], normalize_embeddings=True)[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    g_embs = np.asarray(encoder.encode(generated, normalize_embeddings=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sims = [float(q_emb @ g_emb) for g_emb in g_embs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sum(sims) / len(sims)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "If the answer implies different questions than the one asked, relevance drops."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: G-Eval custom metric"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from deepeval.metrics import GEval"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from deepeval.test_case import LLMTestCaseParams, LLMTestCase"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "metric = GEval("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    name=\"Correctness\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    criteria=\"The answer should be factually accurate and match the expected output.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    evaluation_steps=["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Read the expected output.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Read the actual output.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"List factual claims in the actual output.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"For each claim, mark supported or unsupported by the expected output.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"Return score = fraction supported.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    evaluation_params=[LLMTestCaseParams.INPUT, LLMTestCaseParams.ACTUAL_OUTPUT, LLMTestCaseParams.EXPECTED_OUTPUT],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "test = LLMTestCase(input=\"When was the first iPhone released?\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                   actual_output=\"June 29th, 2007.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                   expected_output=\"June 29, 2007.\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "metric.measure(test)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(metric.score, metric.reason)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The evaluation steps are the rubric. Explicit steps are more stable than implicit \"score 0-1\" prompts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: CI gate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import deepeval"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from deepeval.metrics import FaithfulnessMetric, ContextualRelevancyMetric"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def test_rag_system():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cases = load_regression_cases()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    faith = FaithfulnessMetric(threshold=0.85)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    rel = ContextualRelevancyMetric(threshold=0.7)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for case in cases:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        faith.measure(case)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        assert faith.score >= 0.85, f\"faithfulness regression on {case.id}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        rel.measure(case)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        assert rel.score >= 0.7, f\"relevancy regression on {case.id}\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Ship as a pytest file. Run on every PR. Block merges on regressions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: toy eval from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py`. Stdlib-only approximations of faithfulness (overlap of answer claims with context) and relevance (overlap of answer tokens with question tokens). Not production. Shows the shape."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Use RAGAS on 10 RAG examples with known hallucinations. Verify the faithfulness metric catches each one.\n2. **Medium.** Hand-label 50 QA answers 0-1 for correctness. Score with G-Eval. Measure Spearman rho between judge and human.\n3. **Hard.** Build a pytest CI gate with DeepEval. Intentionally regress the retriever. Verify the gate fails. Add bottom-quantile alerting via threshold check on the lowest 10%."
      ]
    }
